  "adaptations": [
    "The compatibility CLI license comment now points to LICENSE-MIT bundled in the ladyshell-cli package; its MIT license and executable behavior are unchanged.",
    "Audit resources moved into crates/ladyshell/resources/audit for self-contained Cargo archives; resource bytes, upstream hashes and method semantics retained. Repository-relative provenance paths updated.",
    "Workspace Cargo manifest; no upstream release profile in member.",
    "Native ladyshell audit validate commands replace JavaScript invocations.",
    "LADYSHELL.md describes native trust and execution limits.",
    "Embedded development checks use existing authorized sandbox capabilities; isolated audit controls and native evidence remain distinct.",
    "Native bounded audit wave uses isolated connected agents, offline targets, controller-owned receipts and independent verification.",
    "Validator integrated into ladyshell::audit::validator; module imports and fixture include path adjusted, original unsafe-code prohibition retained, imported files marked MIT. Compatibility CLI and tests moved into Ladyshell packages without changing their behavior. Standalone Cargo manifest retired; external dependency requirements retained.",
    "LADYSHELL.md and the Ladyshell introduction in SKILL.md translated into English; authorization, confinement, evidence rules and ladyshell-audit-2 method semantics unchanged."
  ],
